% This is a placeholder for the top-level Simulink model.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical model
% that connects all the subsystems into a complete digital twin.

% The top-level model should implement:
% Excitation Generator -> Cell Model -> Sensor Models -> Parameter Estimator ->
% Excitation Controller -> (feedback to Excitation Generator)
%                             |
%                             v
%                     Decision Engine -> Recovery Power Stage
%
% With proper synchronization and timing between excitation and sensing
%
% Subsystem Connections:
% 1. excitation_generator -> cell_2rc_model (excitation current)
% 2. cell_2rc_model -> {electrical_response, ultrasonic_response, thermal_response} (voltages/currents)
% 3. {electrical_response, ultrasonic_response, thermal_response} -> parameter_estimator (for electrical)
% 4. parameter_estimator -> excitation_controller (uncertainty feedback)
% 5. excitation_controller -> excitation_generator (adaptive parameters)
% 6. excitation_generator -> sensing_timing (trigger synchronization)
% 7. sensing_timing -> {electrical_response, ultrasonic_response, thermal_response} (sample and hold)
% 8. parameter_estimator -> decision_engine (parameter estimates and uncertainties)
% 9. decision_engine -> recovery_power_stage (recovery action commands)
% 10. recovery_power_stage -> cell_2rc_model (balancing currents, if modeling bidirectional flow)
%
% Additional Features:
% - Degradation mode selection (parameter or mask)
% - SOC setting (parameter or mask)
% - Simulation time control
% - Data logging to workspace or file
% - Visualization scopes/dashboard integration
%
% Parameters (recommended to load from workspace or data dictionary):
% - Nominal component values (R0, R1, C1, etc.)
% - Degradation mode scaling factors
% - Excitation pulse nominal parameters
% - Sampling rates and timing
% - Safety limits and thresholds
% - Controller gains (PID, adaptive control)
%
% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink editor to create the graphical model with:
% - Subsystem blocks for each component referenced above
% - Signal routing and connectivity as described
% - Configuration parameters via masks or workspace references
% - Scope blocks for monitoring key signals
% - Proper sample time settings for discrete/continuous components
% - Configuration for fixed-step or variable-step solvers as appropriate